> pet fall down a hole that's in plain sight?  Accually I'm just assuming
> he jumped down the hole because he completely dissapeared and
> I got no message about him dying.  I let him out of my sight for a
> minute and he's gone, and the only thing I can think of that happened
> was that he fell down the hole.

If your tactics was to wait and wait and wait until your dog does
something specific, not only you get bored but also your dog; keep in
mind that they get hungry as you do.

>      other frustrating things that keep happening:
>  - trap doors separate me from my pet

Not unusual that either you or your dog gets separated from the other.
Find the stairs quickly and go up again. Holes are the simpler variant
of getting separated since the direction is clear where you have to
search and they are often just one level below. Worse are level
teleporters once you explored half of the dungeon.

You should also consider to get some tripe (good source is Sokoban)
and tame some other pet if you can't find your first one. Pets come
and go.

>  - my pet eats while I'm getting killed  (I write Elbereth but it's just
> not very reliable when written in the dust)

Solution depends. Is there a crowd of monsters and your pet eats the
first one that is dead? Don't get surrounded! Retreat into a corridor
and let the pet be your shield; then even if he eats his first victim
no critter will pass past him towards you.

>  - my pet just doesn't always attack the monsters that are attacking me
> (even when he's not eating)

Depends on the monster's and the pet's level difference. The pet will
also not attack if he is too low on HP's. Pets are sometimes cleverer
than player characters. ;-)

>  - my pet keeps getting himself killed by the watch captain

If he cannot handle them and you want to keep them lock them away
while you're on the level. (Or lock away the watch people.)

